  "title": "Eth Fundbuero Jetzt Auch Online",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Mass-produced items at ISC",
      "text": "- umbrellas\n\n- hats, gloves, scarves, clothing\n\n- drink bottles, reusable tableware\n\n- toys\n\n- sunglasses (non-corrective)\n\n- writing material\n\nIt’s annoying to lose something. Luckily, items found on ETH premises are usually handed in to the Lost and Found run by the Info + Service Centers (ISC) .\n\nNow ETH has linked up with the Swiss lost property platform easyfind.ch – so you can search online for your valuables at any time, even outside opening hours. You simply create a lost property notice, which is then regularly checked against the lost property handed in."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Mass-produced items at ISC",
      "text": "Lost property found on ETH premises can still be handed in or sought directly at ETH Lost and Found i.e. the ISC desk in the corresponding ETH location. The mass-produced items listed below cannot be recorded online; you should enquire about them at the ISC Lost and Found office:\n\nTo the ETH online lost property service ›"
    }
  ],
